  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pramod @ Dev Kumar Patel vs State Of U.P. on 20 August, 2019 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 78 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 33499 of 2019 Applicant :- Pramod @ Dev Kumar Patel Opposite Party :- State Of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Prabhakar Chandel Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J. Heard learned counsel for the applicant and learned A.G.A. for the State and perused the record.",
    "facts": "The offence under Section 60 of Excise Act is bailable offence and triable by Magistrate. The applicant has been falsely implicated in this case.",
    "arguments": "The submission is that the applicant has been implicated in Section 272 IPC in spite of the coming into force of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Learned A.G.A. opposed the prayer for bail but could not dispute the aforesaid facts as argued by learned counsel for the applicant.",
